      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking tramadol with sertraline can be complicated. Tramadol can increase the risk of serotonin syndrome when combined with SSRIs like sertraline. This rare but serious condition involves symptoms like confusion, hallucinations, or severe headaches. To avoid serious issues, it's best to consult your doctor or healthcare provider for safe advice tailored to your specific situation. They can recommend the safest pain relief options while preventing adverse effects. It’s crucial to prioritize your safety while addressing your back pain.",
      "source": "target",
